            <p>Clarity comes back faster when the body is no longer bracing for another hit. Before you explain, correct, or confront, slow the room down.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="path-card">
            <span class="path-number">2</span>
            <h2>Protect belonging.</h2>
            <p>Children usually soften when they no longer feel forced to prove love, loyalty, or comfort on somebody else’s timeline.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="path-card">
            <span class="path-number">3</span>
            <h2>Get aligned as adults.</h2>
            <p>A stepfamily feels safer when the grown-ups speak privately, decide calmly, and stop making the child carry the emotional weather of the house.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="path-card">
            <span class="path-number">4</span>
            <h2>Choose repair over scorekeeping.</h2>
            <p>Safety grows when someone can say, “That did not go well. Let’s try again more gently,” without humiliation or defending a perfect image.</p>
        </article>
